The study dataset contains multichannel acoustic measurements from 10 anonymous
subjects recorded in a controlled airborne NLOS laboratory environment.

Experimental factors

Subjects: 10 anonymous identities (S1-S10; 5 male and 5 female)
Object configurations: 10 scene codes (0-9)
Postures: standing, sitting, and squatting
Orientations: front, back, right, and left
Excitation conditions: T1-T8 and simultaneous multi-transmitter M
Microphone channels used by the analysis: 8 synchronized channels
Sampling frequency: 44.1 kHz

A fixed subject, object configuration, posture, and orientation defines one
classifier example. For the T1-T8+M configuration, features from nine
multichannel WAV files recordings and eight microphone channels are concatenated.

